The exported [incident page](/kb/incidents/4471) describes one known bug. Its executable views tell a different story: the tenant's date order, booking form and report channel identify distinct problems. This review replaces that single-fix interpretation.

## What the reports support

<SplitSummary />

## Faults and verification

- **Parser:** the shared parser read every date month first. For tenants whose locale writes day first, ambiguous dates swapped day and month. Engineering reports a fix. Verify both day-first and month-first tenants and the app, email and booking-v2 form paths.
- **Hint:** booking-v3 printed `MM/DD/YYYY`, while its form interpreted entries according to a day-first tenant's locale. People following the displayed hint supplied a value the form misread. Engineering retired that form and will not fix it. Confirm that the retired path can no longer take bookings; any replacement must make its hint, example, validation and parser agree.

A fixed parser and a retired form are different outcomes. The timing observations still need checking before assuming that every symptom was addressed. Intake's browser-derived tag is a guess; it does not replace the tenant directory. Unknown tenants stay unplaced for investigation.

## The queue records two different events

<QueueTimeline ticket={4471} />

The reports were exported on 4 October 2026. They are not the live queue; the later engineering disposition is recorded separately above. Re-export before claiming current report totals. These components deduplicate by report ID, filter ticket membership and recompute from the data supplied at the next build. Repeated subjects and overlapping export pages must not inflate the count.

## Triage by evidence

Read the report, resolve its tenant, inspect the booking form and channel, and compare causes before merging. A matching subject alone proves neither a shared cause nor a shared fix. When the tenant or cause is unknown, keep the report separate until investigated.

<DedupeExplorer />

[Decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject) is retained unchanged as history. [Proposed decision 0002](/kb/decisions/0002-dedupe-by-cause) explains the replacement; the support desk must approve the operational policy.

## Evidence and boundaries

The report export, tenant directory, `causes.ts`, `locales.ts`, desk notes and executable views support this review. Report bodies are observations; tenant-based groups are the supplied desk classification. Engineering's later update supplies the closure outcomes. I have not independently verified its production fix or retirement; the timing anomalies remain documented for follow-up.

